 in University. As you know, I like to keep my degree and photography separate but I spent the day in a Letterpress workshop designing, laying out and printing my own "magazine". Whilst on my lunch break I took the time to set this movable type up into a smiley face with the D making a big open smile of a mouth and the colon becoming the eyes. Yellow was the chosen colour of ink for the wooden type face because this is the colour of the majority of modern "emoticons" - :D like that for example. This photograph is meant to link the old letterpress / movable type printing of the industrial revolution with the modern symbol of the internet / digital revolution.\n\nThe hard part of the above image was the photography. I took the photograph, went home, printed it A4 and it looked blurred. So I went back into the studio with my tripod and played with my settings. In the end it worked out at being captured with an Aperture of f/25 and a shutter speed of half a second, the ISO was at 400 with the lens at a focal length of 85mm, not that many will be interested in such details but it has come to my attention that readers are requesting such information more and more. I do need to look into a way of having camera data on every image...wow, I'll be busy!\n\nThe above image was designed to be the front cover of my "magazine" and it was to be called "D-Face", face relating to the typeface and D relating to the symbol and the fact I was defacing the type to make it into a logo, which seems to remind me of the Edwud logo somehow.<|end|>         18
19            3                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Letterpress Type Smiley D-Face\n\nby Ed OKeeffe in ,\n\nLetterpress Type Smiley D-Face Another experimental photograph, the above image was taken today in University. As you know, I like to keep my degree and photography separate but I spent the day in a Letterpress workshop designing, laying out and printing my own "magazine". Whilst on my lunch break I took the time to set this movable type up into a smiley face with the D making a big open smile of a mouth and the colon becoming the eyes. Yellow was the chosen colour of ink for the wooden type face because this is the colour of the majority of modern "emoticons" - :D like that for example. This photograph is meant to link the old letterpress / movable type printing of the industrial revolution with the modern symbol of the internet / digital revolution.\n\nThe hard part of the above image was the photography. I took the photograph, went home, printed it A4 and it looked blurred. So I went back into the studio with my tripod and played with my settings. In the end it worked out at being captured with an Aperture of f/25 and a shutter speed of half a second, the ISO was at 400 with the lens at a focal length of 85mm, not that many will be interested in such details but it has come to my attention that readers are requesting such information more and more. I do need to look into a way of having camera data on every image...wow, I'll be busy!\n\nThe above image was designed to be the front cover of my "magazine" and it was to be called "D-Face", face relating to the typeface and D relating to the symbol and the fact I was defacing the type to make it into a logo, which seems to remind me of the Edwud logo somehow.  assistant                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     <|start|>assistant<|channel|>final<|message|>Letterpress Type Smiley D-Face\n\nby Ed OKeeffe in ,\n\nLetterpress Type Smiley D-Face Another experimental photograph, the above image was taken today in University. As you know, I like to keep my degree and photography separate but I spent the day in a Letterpress workshop designing, laying out and printing my own "magazine". Whilst on my lunch break I took the time to set this movable type up into a smiley face with the D making a big open smile of a mouth and the colon becoming the eyes. Yellow was the chosen colour of ink for the wooden type face because this is the colour of the majority of modern "emoticons" - :D like that for example. This photograph is meant to link the old letterpress / movable type printing of the industrial revolution with the modern symbol of the internet / digital revolution.\n\nThe hard part of the above image was the photography. I took the photograph, went home, printed it A4 and it looked blurred. So I went back into the studio with my tripod and played with my settings. In the end it worked out at being captured with an Aperture of f/25 and a shutter speed of half a second, the ISO was at 400 with the lens at a focal length of 85mm, not that many will be interested in such details but it has come to my attention that readers are requesting such information more and more. I do need to look into a way of having camera data on every image...wow, I'll be busy!\n\nThe above image was designed to be the front cover of my "magazine" and it was to be called "D-Face", face relating to the typeface and D relating to the symbol and the fact I was defacing the type to make it into a logo, which seems to remind me of the Edwud logo somehow.<|end|>         19
20            4                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           January 28, 2019\n\nHello everyone! This card is for few challenges and the card design was inspired by one of my previous cards. This is a one layer card which involves Masking, Stamping, Ink Blending and Coloring. This card would be perfect for beginners and this card would definitely bring a smile to someone you love! ;)\n\nI started by Masking the 1/3rd portion on the card with a washi tape, stamped the frog from Paper Smooches with Memento Ink which is alcohol friendly. Then Masked the frog off and ink blended the background with Peeled Paint Distress Ink. Then I colored the image with Sizzix Markers and finished the card with a sentiment. To create more interest to the card I added splatters of black ink and Stardust Stickles to the pouty lips of the frog! LOL!\n\nI'm entering this card AAA cards CAS Game #132 - Up To One Third + Masking, CASology Week 328: SMILE and Paper Smooches January 2019: ANYTHING GOES challenge.\n\n  1. Wonderfully original and I love it! Thanks so much for linking up at AAA Cards, hope to see you playing again soon.\n\n  2. Oh, goodness. This card really made me smile. Fabulous masking and a really sweet design. Thanks so much for playing along at CASology this week.\n\n  3. Cute card I love how simple and clean it is. That's my hardest thing for me to do I tend to throw everything but the kitchen sink on a card. I think open space scares me... Lol\n\n  4. Depth, your sassy, sexy frog cracked me up!! I love her glittery lips and your gorgeous masking and inking. Thanks for playing along with CASology this week!\n\n  5. Deepti, this card definitely makes me smile! Love the bright, happy colors and that whimsical frog is the best! :)\n    Thank you for joining us again over at CASology!\n\n  6. Wow, adorable card! Just love it! Thanks for joining AAA Cards! Hugs Åsa     system                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 <|start|>system<|message|>January 28, 2019\n\nHello everyone! This card is for few challenges and the card design was inspired by one of my previous cards. This is a one layer card which involves Masking, Stamping, Ink Blending and Coloring. This card would be perfect for beginners and this card would definitely bring a smile to someone you love! ;)\n\nI started by Masking the 1/3rd portion on the card with a washi tape, stamped the frog from Paper Smooches with Memento Ink which is alcohol friendly. Then Masked the frog off and ink blended the background with Peeled Paint Distress Ink. Then I colored the image with Sizzix Markers and finished the card with a sentiment. To create more interest to the card I added splatters of black ink and Stardust Stickles to the pouty lips of the frog! LOL!\n\nI'm entering this card AAA cards CAS Game #132 - Up To One Third + Masking, CASology Week 328: SMILE and Paper Smooches January 2019: ANYTHING GOES challenge.\n\n  1. Wonderfully original and I love it! Thanks so much for linking up at AAA Cards, hope to see you playing again soon.\n\n  2. Oh, goodness. This card really made me smile. Fabulous masking and a really sweet design. Thanks so much for playing along at CASology this week.\n\n  3. Cute card I love how simple and clean it is. That's my hardest thing for me to do I tend to throw everything but the kitchen sink on a card. I think open space scares me... Lol\n\n  4. Depth, your sassy, sexy frog cracked me up!! I love her glittery lips and your gorgeous masking and inking. Thanks for playing along with CASology this week!\n\n  5. Deepti, this card definitely makes me smile! Love the bright, happy colors and that whimsical frog is the best! :)\n    Thank you for joining us again over at CASology!\n\n  6. Wow, adorable card! Just love it! Thanks for joining AAA Cards! Hugs Åsa<|end|>         20
